          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
            comes in two broad flavors (apart from the choice of enriching category):
            %em symmetric operads
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/planar+operads"} planar operads
          %p
            Roughly, a planar operad consists of
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            equipped with a suitable notion of compositon, while a
            %em symmetric operad
            in addition is equipped with a compatible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_n
            on the set (or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            in the enriching category) of
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            of symmetric operads is then a morphism of planar operads that in addition respects this action.
          %p
            The extra “symmetry” structure carried by symmetric operads is crucial for the behaviour of the category of operads in many applications (see the examples below). Notice that it does not so much affect the idea of what a single operad is. In particular, symmetric operads are not restricted to encoding algebraic symmetric structures with symmetric
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_n
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+action"} acts freely
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            The central example illustrating this are the operads
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Comm"} Comm
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Assoc"} Assoc
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Comm"} Comm
            has the singleton set in each degree, with
            %em trivial
            = succeed "-action," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Assoc"} Assoc
            has
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_n
            in each degree, freely acting on itself.
          %p
            Therefore
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Comm"} Comm
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of symmetric operads (while
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Assoc"} Assoc
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/planar+operad"} planar operad
          %p
            Multi-coured symmetric operads are equivalently known also as
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+multicategories"} symmetric multicategories
          %h2#structures_on_the_category_of_symmetric_operads Structures on the category of symmetric operads
          %h3#boardmanvogt_tensor_product Boardman-Vogt tensor product
          %p
            The category of symmetric operads becomes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            for the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boardman-Vogt+tensor+product"} Boardman-Vogt tensor product
          %h3#model_structure Model structure
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            a suitable
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+operads"} model structure on operads
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_categories Relation to categories
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              may be regarded as a coloured symmetric operation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_!(C)
              over set, with the objects of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and colours, and with only unary operation, these being the morphisms in the category
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi n
                    %mo ;
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi C
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi c
                                %mn 1
                              %mo ,
                              %mi c
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mi if
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mi n
                              %mo =
                              %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi ∅
                            %mtd
                              %mi otherwise
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    j_!(C)(c_1, \cdots, c_n ; c)
                    \=
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    C(c_1, c) &amp; if \, n = 1
                    \\\
                    \\emptyset &amp; otherwise
                    }
                    \\right.
                    \\,.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              This
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mo !
                    %mo :
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo →
                    %mi Operad
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_! : Cat \to Operad
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi j
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %mi Operad
                    %mo →
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j^* : Operad \to Cat
              which sends an operad to the underlying category obtained by discarding all
              = succeed "-ary" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≠
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \neq 1
            %p
              There is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi j
                        %mo !
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi id
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j * j_! \simeq id
          %p
            By the discussion at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
            this exhibits a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+subcategory"} coreflective subcategory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo ←
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi j
                          %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi j
                          %mo !
                  %mi Operad
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Cat
                  \\stackrel{\overset{j_!}{\hookrightarrow}}{\underset{j^*}{\leftarrow}}
                  Operad
                  \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
              denote the symmetric operad with a single colour and no non-identity operation. Then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Operad"} Operad
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
              is equivalent to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Operad
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi η
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Cat \simeq Operad_{/\eta}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Because a morphism of operads
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi η
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to \eta
              can exists precisely if there are no operations of arity other than 1 in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            %p
              Under this identification the fuctor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_!
              is the canonical projection out of the slice category
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mo !
                    %mo :
                    %mi Cat
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Operad
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi η
                    %mo →
                    %mi Operad
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    j_! : Cat \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} Operad_{/\eta} \to Operad
                    \\,.
          %p
            For more on this see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+set"} dendroidal set
            the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/dendroidal%20set#FullDiagram"} The full diagram of relations
          %h3#RelationToPlanarOperads Relation to planar operads
          %p
            There is an evident
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo :
                  %mi SymmetricOperad
                  %mo →
                  %mi PlanarOperad
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  U : SymmetricOperad \to PlanarOperad
          %p
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/planar+operads"} planar operads
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+groups"} symmetric groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Symm
                  %mo :
                  %mi PlanarOperad
                  %mo →
                  %mi SymmetricOperad
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Symm : PlanarOperad \to SymmetricOperad
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free construction
            freely adds symmetric group actions.
          %p
            For instance as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/planar+operad"} planar operad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Assoc"} Assoc
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            (has the point in each degree). Its symmetrization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Symm
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Assoc
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Symm(Assoc)
            is still the operad for associative
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoids"} monoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_n
            in degree
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SymmetricOperad
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SymmetricOperad
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Comm"} Comm
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#in_
            In
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
          %p
            We list some examples of
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                For every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism+operad"} endomorphism operad
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi End
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} End(C)
              %p This establishes a reflective (but non-full) inclusion
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi End
                      %mo :
                      %mi SymmMonCat
                      %mo →
                      %mi SymmOperad
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      End : SymmMonCat \to SymmOperad
              %p and makes precise the way in which a (symmetric) operad is a generalization of a (symmetric) monoidal category.
              %p
                For any other symmetric operad
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo →
                      %mi End
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      P \to End(C)
              %p
                is precisely an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+an+operad"} algebra over an operad
                over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              %p
                The operad
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Comm"} Comm
                for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoids"} commutative monoids
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
                in symmetric
                = succeed "-operads," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo =
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V =
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              %p
                It has a single
                = succeed "-ary" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
                necessarily acting trivially in each degree.
              %p A morphism of operads
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi Comm
                      %mo →
                      %mi End
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Vect
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      A : Comm \to End(Vect)
              %p
                is precisely a commutative and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
                structure on a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            %li
              %p
                The operad
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Assoc"} Assoc
                for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoids"} monoids
                is, as a symmetric operad, the one with a single colour that has precisely
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo !
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n!
                many operations in degree
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
                acting freely on these.
              %p
                This means that there is a single
                = succeed "-ary" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %p A morphism of operads
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Assoc
                      %mo →
                      %mi End
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Vect
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      Assoc \to End(Vect)
              %p
                is precisely an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
                on a vector space.
            %li
              %p
                For every
                %em
                  non-planar finite rooted
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree"} tree
                there is a symmetric operad freely generated by it. For more on this see the section
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/dendroidal+set#Trees"} Trees and free operads
                at
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+set"} dendroidal set
          %h3#in__2
            In
